ios: drag-to-scroll lists and the chat history

A drag that starts vertically on the content of a scrollable interface layer (side panel lists such
as quests/friends/ignore, main modals such as the bank, chat modals) or on the chat history scrolls
it, the content following the finger, instead of emulating a held left button (upstream only scrolled
through the 16 px scrollbars, about 12 pt wide on an iPhone, and a drag on the chat text clicked at
the release point). Horizontal-first drags keep the left-button emulation (moving items, dragging a
scrollbar), as does a drag that starts on a layer's scrollbar column. Releasing never clicks.

